        "original_id": "b3cd5395-5454-50f3-9e8d-ed521b41f086",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Patsy Mink, Arlene Horowitz\n- Laws: Women's Educational Equity Act, Public Law 93-380\n- Places: Hawaii\n- Roles: Congresswoman, staff assistant, American politician\n\nFacts:\n- Patsy Matsu Takemoto Mink was born on December 6, 1927, and she was an American politician from Hawaii.\n- Patsy Mink was a third-generation Japanese American and a member of the Democratic Party.\n- The Women's Educational Equity Act was enacted as Section 513 of Public Law 93-380.\n- Congresswoman Patsy Mink of Hawaii introduced the Women's Educational Equity Act in the United States House of Representatives.\n- Arlene Horowitz, a staff assistant to the education subcommittee on which Patsy Mink served, conceived and drafted the Women's Educational Equity Act.\n- Patsy Matsu Takemoto Mink died on September 28, 2002.",
